  ],
  "fact_notes": [
    "人物・出来事・制度は架空の教材例。実在の調査・統計・実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A fictional art museum prepared an exhibition of photographs taken by residents of a changing neighborhood.",
          "ja": "架空の美術館は変化する地域の住民が撮影した写真展を準備した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The curator intended to show everyday experiences rather than select only technically impressive images.",
          "ja": "学芸員は技術的に優れた画像だけでなく日常の経験を示すつもりだった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Some residents submitted photographs of demolished buildings, while others recorded activities that continued despite redevelopment.",
          "ja": "取り壊された建物の写真を出す人もいれば再開発後も続く活動を記録する人もいた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The collection nevertheless contained almost no pictures from residents who had moved away.",
          "ja": "それでも転居した住民からの写真はほとんどなかった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The curator considered asking an artist to reconstruct scenes that were absent from the photographic record.",
          "ja": "学芸員は写真記録にない場面を芸術家に再構成してもらうことを考えた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Although such illustrations could communicate experiences that were otherwise difficult to imagine, they would not constitute documentary evidence of particular events.",
          "ja": "イラストは想像しにくい経験を伝え得るが、特定の出来事の記録的証拠にはならない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She worried that placing reconstructed scenes beside original photographs without explanation could create misleading impressions.",
          "ja": "説明なく再構成した場面を元の写真の隣に置くと誤解を招くと心配した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The exhibition therefore identified the sources and distinct purposes of any representations it included.",
          "ja": "そこで展示に含む表現の出所と異なる目的を明示した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "One artist suggested deliberately displaying an empty frame with a short label explaining whose perspectives were missing.",
          "ja": "一人の芸術家は欠けている視点を説明する短いラベルを付けた空の額縁を意図的に展示する案を出した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Rather than pretending that the museum could fully represent the community, the exhibit would acknowledge a limitation of its collection.",
          "ja": "地域全体を完全に代表できると装わず、資料の限界を認める展示になる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The label invited visitors to consider why certain experiences might be difficult for institutions to preserve.",
          "ja": "ラベルは特定の経験が施設で保存しにくい理由を考えるよう促した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It also provided information about how former residents could voluntarily contribute additional material in the future.",
          "ja": "元住民が今後自発的に資料を提供する方法も示した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Visitors responded differently to the empty frame during a preliminary viewing.",
          "ja": "予備鑑賞では空の額縁への反応はさまざまだった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Some appreciated its acknowledgment of missing voices, whereas others initially misunderstood it as an unfinished installation.",
          "ja": "欠けた声を認める姿勢を評価する人もいれば、当初は未完成の展示と誤解する人もいた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The museum revised the accompanying explanation rather than assuming that an ambiguous artistic gesture would automatically communicate its intended meaning.",
          "ja": "曖昧な芸術的表現が意図を自動的に伝えると考えず、説明を修正した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The curator retained the frame because it raised a question that a conventional display of additional images might have concealed.",
          "ja": "普通に画像を追加すると隠れるかもしれない問いを提起するため額縁を残した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "An exhibition inevitably involves choices about what to include and how to arrange it.",
          "ja": "展覧会には必然的に何を含みどう配置するかの選択が伴う。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Its quality does not always depend on eliminating every visible gap in the presentation.",
          "ja": "質は必ずしも提示の空白を全てなくすことには依存しない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "An explicit acknowledgment of absence can sometimes invite more thoughtful interpretation than an apparently complete representation.",
          "ja": "欠落を明示することで一見完全な表現より思慮深い解釈を促すこともある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The empty frame became a reminder that an artistic account could be meaningful without claiming to be comprehensive.",
          "ja": "空の額縁は芸術的記述が包括的だと主張せずとも意義を持てるというしるしになった。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
